{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cgbn98hJEW8t7XxfSF38P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 10 is done, marked `[x]`, with the gate passed and nothing committed.\n\n**What is proved.** The first-moment floor holds for the padded generator with the sizes the table has before the repairs. The pads only add ones under a coupling with explicit auxiliary randomness, so an empty pair of the padded graph is one of the base graph and pathwidth can only rise. In the patterns-first pad order the rows after the pattern pad are exactly uniform sets of size `max(s, 2)`, so the truncated-size bound is a theorem there, and a Chernoff typical-set argument gives a quenched form of both. All six statements were brute-force checked before being stated: 205 rational identities, two full enumerations, 40,000 coupled draws at eight customers with every pair and every pathwidth compared.\n\n**What is not.** The rejection is not an increasing event of the base entries. One added entry makes a pad vanish on 40% of additions at `d = 2`, loses the acceptance on 0.7% and lowers the padded pathwidth on 3.5%, so Harris–FKG does not apply to it. The item ends, as its kill criterion allows, with the `1 / P(accepted)` form and the acceptance measured per class. The two Harris forms that are rigorous add nothing in practice. The realised-size inequality stays measured.\n\n**The numbers.** The proved 0.01 floors are more than one stack below the measured-model floors on 35 of 40 classes. At `d = 2` they are trivial in the Bernoulli form because 40% of base patterns have at most one customer. At `d ≥ 4` the gap is the annealing, not the pads, and the quenched form buys back 2 to 4 stacks on the largest classes. The acceptance factor moves no floor on any class. No certified optimum lies below any rigorous floor.\n\n**Deliverables.** Section 10 of `reports/excess_phase_diagram.md` with every table, the library section in `learning/first_moment.py` with 13 new tests, `reports/scratch/validity/` with the check script and logs, the replaced paragraph in Appendix E of the paper, and the PROGRESS.md entry with notes for items 11 and 12."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1205,"cache_read_input_tokens":312322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1205,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":707,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec075f6c-5313-4bc9-8854-91bff469a12d","uuid":"5f271a38-f4ce-420b-864a-609b2a0b9928","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:02:12.548Z","request_id":"req_011Cgbn98KEGHZBJUoEpCzqy"}
